---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/url';
---

<Layout title="Scales & Arpeggios">
	<main class="wrap">
		<nav style="font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:1rem;"><a href={url("reference/")}>← all reference</a></nav>
		<article class="course-article">
			<h1>Scales &amp; arpeggios</h1>
			<p class="muted">The map that serves the setlist. Each scale is tied to the songs that need it.</p>

			<h2>E minor pentatonic</h2>
			<p>Plush, Wicked Garden, Cumbersome, My Own Worst Enemy.</p>
			<div class="tab">E  | G A |
A  | D E |
   (root E — frets 0/2/3 on E string, 0/2 on A string)</div>

			<h2>Blues scale (E)</h2>
			<p>Adds the ♭5 for fills over the pentatonic core.</p>
			<div class="tab">E | G A B♭ B D</div>

			<h2>G major</h2>
			<p>Faithfully (key of G), Say It Ain't So.</p>
			<div class="tab">G A B C D E F♯</div>

			<h2>A minor</h2>
			<p>Interstate Love Song (Am–F–C–G, i–VI–III–VII).</p>
			<div class="tab">A B C D E F G</div>

			<h2>Arpeggios</h2>
			<p>The real bass language — chord tones. Major, minor, dominant 7. DeLeo's lines are built from these.</p>
		</article>
	</main>
</Layout>

<style>
	.course-article {
		max-width: 42rem;
		font-family: Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;
		font-size: 18px;
		line-height: 1.65;
	}
	.course-article .tab {
		font-family: 'SF Mono', ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
		white-space: pre;
		background: var(--panel-2);
		border: 1px solid var(--rule);
		border-radius: 6px;
		padding: 1rem 1.2rem;
		overflow-x: auto;
		line-height: 1.7;
		display: block;
		margin: 0.5rem 0 1.25rem;
	}
</style>
